  "verbalization": "Traxillagenin appears to have a dual mechanism of action targeting VMRC-MELG, with evidence suggesting it interacts with both the T-cell surface glycoprotein CD3 and Lup-20(29)-en-3-ol, (3beta)-, which in turn targets VMRC-MELG. This indicates that Traxillagenin may act through a pathway involving the immune system, specifically by inhibiting T-cell surface proteins that are involved in immune signaling. The presence of multiple overlapping targets suggests a potential role in modulating immune responses, possibly through the inhibition of T-cell activation or function. The integration of these pathways highlights the possibility that Traxillagenin could exert its effects by interfering with key components of the immune system, thereby influencing the activity of VMRC-MELG. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Traxillagenin and VMRC-MELG, though further investigation is needed to confirm the precise mode of action and the biological relevance of these interactions.",
